{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsubNQA6sm7xq7MEJEy7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"v8F drops to 91/128 from v8E's 97, so the snapback change doesn't help; v8E stays the candidate. One consideration: if the practice games use fixed random streams, two networks differing only in rare situations play identical games until the first divergence. That would make small A/B tests paired and more informative. Let me check that between v8E and v8F.\n\n```python\nimport json, numpy as np\nGE=json.load(open('/work/pass_22/games.json')); GF=json.load(open('/work/pass_23/games.json'))\nsame=0; diverge=[]\nfor a,b in zip(GE,GF):\n    ma=[m['move'] for m in a['moves']]; mb=[m['move'] for m in b['moves']]\n    if ma==mb: same+=1\n    else:\n        k=next(i for i,(x,y) in enumerate(zip(ma,mb)) if x!=y) if any(x!=y for x,y in zip(ma,mb)) else min(len(ma),len(mb))\n        diverge.append((k,a['result'],b['result']))\nprint('identical games',same,'of',len(GE))\nprint('divergent games: E wins',sum(1 for k,r1,r2 in diverge if r1>0),'F wins',sum(1 for k,r1,r2 in diverge if r2>0),'n',len(diverge))\nprint('first divergence plies',sorted(k for k,_,_ in diverge)[:40])\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":474733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":678},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fea22f52-dc2f-44b9-a9cd-4bab4d2abe73","uuid":"baa66817-1771-4599-b35a-ef95b1f5eefc","timestamp":"2026-11-09T19:29:59.703Z","request_id":"req_011CgsubK8SeLhcXrsWooEMs"}
